<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Pep Boys cut to intermediate.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Pep Boys cut to intermediate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch cut its rating on Pep Boys -- Manny, Moe &amp; Jack to neutral from accumulate on an intermediate basis.</p>
<p>-- The stock remains a long-term accumulate, the brokerage said.</p>
<p>-- Shares were indicated sharply lower, ahead of their opening on the New York Stock Exchange, at between $26 and $28 from their Thursday closing level of 33-1/16.  </p>
<p>-- Analyst Peter Caruso was not immediately available for comment.</p>
